# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — The Last Thread (Godot 4 .NET / mono project)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RULE OF THUMB for Godot:
#   - IGNORE  ".godot/"      -> the editor's import CACHE; it rebuilds itself.
#   - COMMIT  "*.import"     -> the per-asset import files next to each PNG.
#                               These store the UIDs your .tscn scenes point at.
#                               If you ignore these, scenes break for collaborators!
#   - COMMIT  "addons/"      -> third-party addons (Dialogue Manager) so teammates
#                               get them automatically.
# =============================================================================

# --- Godot 4 editor cache (regenerated on open) ---
.godot/
/android/

# --- .NET / C# build artifacts (this is a Mono/.NET project) ---
# Godot regenerates the solution/project files and these build folders, so they
# don't belong in version control.
.mono/
bin/
obj/
*.csproj.user
*.sln.user

# --- Exported game builds (don't commit compiled output) ---
# If you export to one of these folders, it stays off GitHub. Adjust to taste.
/build/
/builds/
/export/
/exports/

# --- Local assistant / editor settings (personal, not shared) ---
# settings.local.json is YOUR machine's local config; collaborators have their own.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- IDE / editor folders ---
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~

# =============================================================================
# NOTE on export_presets.cfg (not present yet):
#   When you set up exporting, Godot creates export_presets.cfg. It's normally
#   fine to commit (collaborators get your export settings) — BUT if you ever add
#   a signing keystore PASSWORD to it, do NOT commit it. If that happens, add this
#   line here:   export_presets.cfg
# =============================================================================
